  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "R1 and R5 strongly support applying ball milling followed by SPS at 1000 °C to transition-metal high-entropy alloy systems, making the later intervention broadly foreseeable. R2–R6 additionally provide related guidance about sintering-driven densification, accelerated diffusion, phase formation, dispersed secondary phases, hardness, and oxidation or corrosion behavior. However, none identifies the MgAlTiVFeCo system or anticipates the specific AlV2O4, FeAl2O4, and FeTiO3 barrier phases, their optimal precipitation at 1000 °C, or their role in producing a dense passive film that blocks chloride penetration. The parabolic, biphasic oxidation mechanism is also not disclosed. Thus the records point toward 1000 °C SPS and beneficial high-temperature microstructural evolution, but the specific oxide-mediated corrosion mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
}
